[SuperEditor][SuperTextField] Clear composing region after selection changes. Resolves #1685

When an IME popover is visible, like the Japanese character picker, tapping somewhere else in the editor doesn't close the IME popover.

The reason is that we change the selection, but keep the composing region. To solve that, we need to clear the composing region after the selection changes.

This PR changes the places where we change the selection to also issue a `ChangeComposingRegionRequest`. `SuperTextField` was also modified to clear the composing region.

Initially I added the `ChangeComposingRegionRequest` in the same batch as the selection change request. This caused 
some tests to fail because `AdjustSelectionAroundTagReaction` expects a selection change as the only change in the changelist:

```dart
if (changeList.length > 1 || changeList.first is! SelectionChangeEvent) {
  // We only want to move the caret when we're confident about what changed. Therefore,
  // we only react to changes that are solely a selection change, i.e., we ignore
  // situations like text entry, text deletion, etc.
  editorStableTagsLog.info(" - change list isn't just a single SelectionChangeEvent: $changeList");
  return;
}
```

I changed the implementation to issue the `ChangeComposingRegionRequest` in a separate request, but I think it would probably be better if the change `AdjustSelectionAroundTagReaction` to handle the case where we have a selection change and a composing region change in the list.

